{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"C1: Dropping “disjoint”","title_html":"C1: Dropping “disjoint”","html":"<p><span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"prp-disjoint-cycles-commute\">@prp-disjoint-cycles-commute</span>\nassumes that the supports are disjoint.</p>\n<div class=\"enumerate\" data-options=\"label=(\\alph*)\">\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>Find two transpositions that share exactly one point and do not\ncommute.</li>\n<li>Find two cycles in <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"S_3\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D446 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.032em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> with the\n<strong>same</strong> support that do commute.</li>\n<li>In the proof of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"prp-disjoint-cycles-commute\">@prp-disjoint-cycles-commute</span>,\nwhich step fails for the pair of (a)?</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch3/permutations-and-cycles.html"}